# MY OWN VERIFICATION CAPTURES — 80 folders, 4.8 GB, and every byte of it was
# riding along in `genex preview`'s source push. That is almost certainly what
# "✗ Couldn't save your game's source" was: the build deploys fine (it is built
# from src/ and public/), then the source push tries to move nearly five
# gigabytes of PNG through git-lfs and gives up, and the publish that follows
# 409s with "No uploaded build for this commit".
#
# Nothing in the game reads this directory — checked, it appears only in prose.
# The files stay on disk; they are just not part of the game's source any more.
# Regenerable by definition: they are screenshots of the game.
shots/

# Scratch left over from a debugging session, one of them empty.
before.txt
err.txt

# Embedded git repos — reference clones, not part of this game.
.claude/reference/ez-tree/
.claude/skills/img2threejs/

